  "releaseNotes": "Kafka, RabbitMQ and Playwright: the assertions chain before the await, as in HTTP since 6.8.0: await Given()...ExecuteAsync().AssertSuccess(). They are generated from each builder, so every public method has its counterpart on the Task. Playwright: ExpectFetchStatus(200) checks the status of a FetchFromPage step before the last one of a scenario, and stops it there. Additive: no code changes needed from 6.10.1. Upgrade guide: https://github.com/andrewBezerra/xunit-assured-net/blob/main/UPGRADING.md",
